==Bikeways==
Some examples of the types of [[Cycling infrastructure#Bikeway types|bikeways]] under the purview of bicycle transportation engineers include [[Cycling infrastructure#Separated in-roadway bikeway|partially segregated infrastructure in-road]] such as [[bike lane]]s, buffered bike lanes; [[Cycling infrastructure#Physically separated in-roadway bikeway|physically segregated in-road]] such as [[cycle track]]s; [[bike path]]s with their own right-of-way; and [[Cycling infrastructure#Shared in-roadway bikeways|shared facilities]] such as bicycle boulevards, shared lane markings, advisory bike lane, road shoulders, wide outside lanes, [[shared space|shared street]] schemes, and any roadways with legal access for cycling.

===In roadway===
{{see|Bikeway safety}}
[[NACTO]] guidelines state "desired width for a cycle track should be 5 feet (1.5 m). In areas with high bicyclist volumes or uphill sections, the desired width should be 7 feet (2.1 m)".
CROW standard width for one way cycle paths in the Netherlands is a minimum of 2.5 m (8′). For bidirectional use the minimum is 3.5 m (11′).

